 "cards": [
  {
   "dot": "cyan",
   "items": [
    "A write touches exactly one base shard, and the local entry commits in the same shard transaction",
    "A term lookup without the record id fans out to all 4 shards: 4 RPCs, then a merge",
    "Tail latency follows the slowest shard; adding shards grows storage, not query throughput"
   ],
   "title": "Local: cheap writes, scatter reads"
  },
  {
   "dot": "emerald",
   "items": [
    "The global index is sharded by term across 2 index shards; one record's write fans out to 1 base plus up to 2 index shards",
    "Index writes travel asynchronously through an outbox relay, versioned per record, so a crash replays them",
    "A single-term read touches 1 index shard plus the base shards holding the matches; two terms intersect over the network"
   ],
   "title": "Global: targeted reads, fanned-out writes"
  },
  {
   "dot": "rose",
   "items": [
    "A multi-term write can land partially: the AND query then misses the record — a false negative, counted in the demo",
    "A deleted record can linger in the index: the reader revalidates every id against the base, and the delete wins",
    "Tripwires: fan-out equal to shard count, index lag per term, and a tombstone before any index purge"
   ],
   "title": "Staleness and tripwires"
  }
 ],
